  "doi": "10.21203/rs.3.rs-2659802/v1",
  "summary_of_paper_contents": "Sections 2-3 prove four 1-step/2-step preimage equivalence relations (Propositions 3.1-3.4) in bases 3 <= b <= 10 showing phi(a) = phi(x) or phi^2(a) = phi^2(x) when adding b^(l-1)-1, (b-1)*b^(l/2-1), or sum_{k=1}^{l-3} (b-1)*b^k. Section 4 Case 1 gives an explicit template cycle only in base b = 4 (a power of 2, already known) for a = 3333_4 = 255. Section 4 Case 2 and Section 5 apply Propositions 3.1-3.4 in base b = 10 to unproved Lychrel candidates (196, 879, 1997, 7059) to generate sibling candidates (e.g. 4994, 8778, 19723, 89760, 58883, 43593) tested numerically to 530,914 iterations without any template-closure proof.",
